.TH accton 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
accton \- turn process accounting on or off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B accton
[\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With a
.IR file ,
.B accton
tells the kernel to append a record to it as each process exits: the
name, the time it used, and who ran it.  With no argument, accounting is
turned off.
.SH NOTES
Only the superuser may do this, and the file must already exist.
.PP
The file grows without limit while accounting is on.  On a card that
matters; truncate or remove it from time to time.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ac (1),
.BR ps (1)
